// Dominican OS — re-assert branding after any package transaction.
//
// Why this exists: several branded files sit at paths owned by packages
// (base-files ships /etc/os-release, for example). The dpkg diversions
// registered by apply-branding.sh protect those, but an update can still
// replace a theme asset, regenerate a schema override, or install a package
// that ships its own copy of one of our files. Rather than hope that never
// happens, re-apply the cheap parts of the branding automatically.
//
// The hook is a no-op on systems where /usr/share/dct-os is absent, so this
// file is harmless if the payload is ever removed.
//
// To watch it work:  sudo apt install --reinstall base-files
//                    cat /etc/os-release | head -2

DPkg::Post-Invoke { "/usr/sbin/dct-rebrand --quiet || true"; };
